The kept-controls list doesn't need these ids, because 'near' and 'angle' were never in it. Add a shots.js check for duplicate ids with the element open on every tab pair. Decide whether Wrestle > Throw keeps sharing state.angle with Rex's Throw tab now that both are on screen together, and note the decision in the PR.

Mark the element stale whenever a redraw is skipped because it is closed, and show the placeholder on reopening when it is stale:
let duoQueued = false, duoKeepAll = true, duoGen = 0, duoStale = false;
function scheduleDuo(keepControls) { if (!state.duoOpen) { duoStale = true; return; } ... }
function renderDuo(keepControls) { if (!state.duoOpen) { duoStale = true; return; } duoStale = false; duoMode = true; ... }
In the toggle handler: if (state.duoOpen) { if (!$('#duo-bay').firstChild || duoStale) $('#duo-bay').replaceChildren(el('p', { class: 'muted', text: 'Working it out…' })); scheduleDuo(false); }
This is simpler and more reliable than comparing JSON.stringify(state), because state includes keys unrelated to the two-player tests.

